   "fault": "The key 'bees' echoes the stem word 'beekeeper' (bee- is spelled out in the question), so a child can pick it by matching letters without finding the shepherd-looks-after-sheep relationship. Neither distractor (sting, wool) shares that echo.",
   "objective": true,
   "suggestedFix": "Use a stem whose second term does not contain the key, e.g. 'shepherd is to sheep as swineherd/farmer is to ...', or keep beekeeper and accept the echo only if every option echoes equally."
