   "faultAt": [
    "option crop",
    "execution"
   ],
   "fault": "'crop' is close to defensible: famine is commonly explained to children as a time when crops fail, so 'drought is a lack of rain, famine is a lack of crops' is a reasonable reading. The execution does not say why crop is wrong, only that it is 'not a lack of crop in the way the pair works'.",
   "objective": false,
   "suggestedFix": "Replace crop with a same-topic word that cannot be read as what is lacking, e.g. 'hunger' or 'farmer'."
